Subject: [PATCH] gui_test: read keys from /dev/input/linht-keys when linht-shelld runs

linht-shelld grabs the raw keypad and forwards keys on the virtual device
/dev/input/linht-keys. Use it when present, otherwise keep reading the keypad
directly, so the image works with and without linht-shelld.

When the key device goes away (linht-shelld stopped or crashed), the kernel
drops the queued key releases and read() fails with ENODEV, so a held PTT
would never be released. Leave the main loop then, so the cleanup puts the
radio back to receive.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [interim: the LVGL Radio app replaces gui_test, docs/architecture.md D30]
---
--- a/tests/gui_test/test.c
+++ b/tests/gui_test/test.c
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#include <errno.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <stdint.h>
@@ -893,7 +894,9 @@ int main(void)
 		fprintf(stderr, "Database initialization failed. Check permissions or path.\n");
 	}
 
-	// keyboard
+	// keyboard: linht-shelld forwards the keypad on /dev/input/linht-keys; without it, read the keypad directly
+	if (access("/dev/input/linht-keys", R_OK) == 0)
+		kbd_path = "/dev/input/linht-keys";
 	if ((rval = kbd_init(&kbd, kbd_path)) != 0)
 	{
 		return rval;
@@ -1072,6 +1075,8 @@ int main(void)
 		// check keypad events
 		struct input_event ev;
 		ssize_t n = read(kbd, &ev, sizeof(ev)); // non-blocking
+		if (n < 0 && errno == ENODEV) // linht-shelld is gone with linht-keys: no PTT release can arrive
+			break;
 		if (n == (ssize_t)sizeof(ev) && ev.type == EV_KEY)
 		{
 			if (ev.value == KEY_PRESS)
